<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-11348] Ping node procedure may fail when another node leaves the cluster</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11348</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Additional pinging of node on join implemented in &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5569&quot; title=&quot;TCP Discovery SPI allows multiple NODE_JOINED / NODE_FAILED leading to a cluster DDoS&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5569&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5569&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; may incorrectly fail leading to shutting down joining node.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The reason for this is that if another node from the same host bound to the same discovery port as joining node has left the cluster right before joining node, socket used for pinging gets closed.&lt;br/&gt;
This leads to the situation when pinging node considers joining node as &quot;unreachable&quot; and fails it with JOIN_IMPOSSIBLE error code.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Workaround: simply start again node failed on join.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
